From: Jimmi Dyson <464659+jimmidyson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:18:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(test): drive Machines to Running against workloadsim in
 simrun

simrun starts workloadsim as a fourth process next to ntnx-sim, the core
manager and the CAPX manager. workloadsim fakes the workload cluster: an
API server at each Cluster's declared endpoint and a Node per Machine
carrying the providerID CAPX reported, and it writes the cluster's CA and
kubeconfig since no control plane provider runs here. The endpoint moves
from a placeholder to 127.0.0.1:20000, inside workloadsim's port range,
and the run waits for Running rather than Provisioned.

--control-plane-machines labels the first N Machines as control plane, so
their Nodes are labelled and tainted and the Cluster reports its control
plane initialized. make test-sim installs workloadsim from
kcp-cluster-api; WORKLOADSIM_REF picks the branch or tag.
